  "body": "Step 5 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#initialise-the-document-object says:\r\n\r\n> If browsingContext's only entry in its session history is the initial about:blank Document that was added when that browsing context was created, and navigationParams's history handling is \"replace\", and that Document's origin is same origin-domain with navigationParams's origin, then do nothing.\r\n\r\nI can't tell what conditions would trigger this step. As per https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-origin, an `about:blank` has a new unique opaque origin, which is not same-origin or same-origin-domain with any other opaque origin besides itself. At first I though that this means the only way you could trigger this step is if we create a new top-level browsing context group which contains the `about:blank` document, and invoke `location.replace(document.URL)`, but come to think of it, I think that wouldn't even trigger this step because the origins of the two `about:blank` URLs would have distinct opaque origins, and would not be considered [same-origin-domain](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#same-origin-domain).\r\n\r\nSo the question remains: how do you trigger this step, and what is the purpose of it?\r\n\r\ncc @domenic ",
